   "id": "co_capitol_snowmass_traverse",
   "area_id": "co_capitol_peak",
   "name": "Capitol-Snowmass Traverse",
   "grade": "5.7",
   "discipline": "alpine",
   "overview": "Colorado's most demanding link between two fourteeners, joining Capitol Peak with Snowmass Mountain across about two and a half miles of Elk Range crest. Nearly all of it is rotten, with gendarmes, exposure, tricky navigation and downclimbs at 4th or 5th class. A common plan is a loop from Snowmass Creek: ascend Capitol by its northeast ridge, then head south, dropping west whenever the crest blocks you. Exits east lead toward Pierre Lake Cirque. Near North Snowmass, an exposed ramp system and a solid pitch past an old piton lead up. Snowmass is 3rd class; descend its East Face. Stay 50 feet from your partner.",
